{"classification":"mathematical-reversed-inequality","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0214","math_ordinal":54,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding argument proves mu-star(-A) <= mu-star(A); applying it to -A supplies the reverse inequality. The printed self-inequality is tautological.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:99","source_normalized_sha256":"f15a48861c4eb22dfd2b0fe6e1b0a202c38d52bdfc7b7f42adb295630fa187c4","source_text":"\\mu^*A\\le\\mu^*(-(-A))=\\mu^*A","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:99","target_normalized_sha256":"cbe874745620b5f6724bbed529afdd86522ca970c2d046f3fa2987150c14b53f","target_text":"\\mu^*A=\\mu^*(-(-A))\\le\\mu^*(-A)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-measure-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0215","math_ordinal":95,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"H1 and H2 are subsets of R^2 and the surrounding paragraph explicitly declares two-dimensional Lebesgue measure mu_2.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:147-148","source_normalized_sha256":"2d34be49f0d1b1f3f9d93dd5b5c67b8f82c0111770a38bd4175630d30524da3b","source_text":"\\mu(\\phi[H_2]\\setminus\\phi[H_1])=\\mu\\phi[H_2\\setminus H_1]=\\mu(H_2\\setminus H_1)=0","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:147-148","target_normalized_sha256":"872bbb2fa1686189011a1cd4e5e7efd7cf42950062f9248862fadd5f6aff7d8d","target_text":"\\mu_2(\\phi[H_2]\\setminus\\phi[H_1])=\\mu_2\\phi[H_2\\setminus H_1]=\\mu_2(H_2\\setminus H_1)=0","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"source-wrong-cross-reference","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0216","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The shear map and its inverse are established in 255A(d)-(e); 255B has only parts (a)-(b). Protected-reference ordinal 17 is ledgered by the unit validator.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:246","source_text":"255B(d-e)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:246","target_text":"255A(d-e)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-representative","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0217","math_ordinal":203,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The function theta(u,v) is defined from representatives f of u and g of v; assigning both representatives to u drops the second argument.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:319","source_normalized_sha256":"b4d15198c1e8cc5357a0a3850059526215738a9f663a1c66ebb6c4be2674d702","source_text":"g^{\\ssbullet}=u","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:319","target_normalized_sha256":"9758bd0821eef40607501239b476d6b25cdef27f2f690e828f682a76c0bfd5b0","target_text":"g^{\\ssbullet}=v","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"source-malformed-norm-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0218","math_ordinal":361,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The middle summand is an Lp norm and lacks its opening double bar in the authority.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:574","source_normalized_sha256":"9e5f9b962e5dd902266d23f6e863ee1ae4e671f54243b410d181c138d1a9e522","source_text":"+|h_x-h_{x'}\\|_p","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:574","target_normalized_sha256":"3f38be53b2fc24cc78cf147d696a1374202581a7348d54d73d37cde02fec6a56","target_text":"+\\|h_x-h_{x'}\\|_p","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"source-malformed-norm-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0219","math_ordinal":362,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Holder's inequality requires the Lp norm of f_x-f_x'; the authority has a single closing bar.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:582","source_normalized_sha256":"11443045cf7144cda20c705ffff611df0e4573768514a2ceca5d2cfed55ea0d1","source_text":"\\|f_x-f_{x'}|_p\\|g\\|_q","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:582","target_normalized_sha256":"0e4c2a186592fa6b5ea56b8073eac5661e6ecf82cacd484e275ae3247145b387","target_text":"\\|f_x-f_{x'}\\|_p\\|g\\|_q","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-coordinate-declaration","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0220","math_ordinal":385,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The displayed product uses beta_ni, so the r-dimensional interval endpoint b_n must receive the coordinate declaration parallel to a_n.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:603-608","source_normalized_sha256":"49aa436030f0526f5bbcc6e2737e906f30f9c9037aadcd1c6447da0fdfe8fa48","source_text":"if I_n=coint{a_n,b_n} ... writing a_n=(alpha_n1,...,alpha_nr)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:603-608","target_normalized_sha256":"5bf758d362fd295004de8b9ce25b1902ff18005b16ffe8873576a342b0a4fb17","target_text":"if I_n=coint{a_n,b_n} ... writing a_n=(alpha_n1,...,alpha_nr), b_n=(beta_n1,...,beta_nr)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"source-malformed-parenthesis","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0221","math_ordinal":473,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The reflected set begins with -(...), but the authority closes only the interval and measure parentheses; the set parenthesis is missing.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:751","source_normalized_sha256":"47c7115d7e879d79274cfd3ba9478bbeb32a24eaa289b6505178d5f3d18e5e28","source_text":"\\mu(-(E\\cap\\ooint{-\\pi,\\pi})","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:751","target_normalized_sha256":"1166bfe1739b39a113e8ed83e929efa7133c8512aac500358263faea735b7fb2","target_text":"\\mu(-(E\\cap\\ooint{-\\pi,\\pi}))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-representative","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0222","math_ordinal":633,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The definition of u*v=w requires g to represent the second input v; w is the output equivalence class.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:931","source_normalized_sha256":"710a1b63ea2e3ad6b97a11cb77158b18fe469e7205ec0ec2b24feedd06500ce2","source_text":"g^{\\ssbullet}=w","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:931","target_normalized_sha256":"9758bd0821eef40607501239b476d6b25cdef27f2f690e828f682a76c0bfd5b0","target_text":"g^{\\ssbullet}=v","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-space-notation","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0223","math_ordinal":642,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The declared complex-valued quotient space is L^0_C throughout the definition; L^0(C) would denote an L0 space over a measure object C.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:933","source_normalized_sha256":"0fe684ace969c29cb22e691c4f6e4e46f448acaff7e11789152ac7a62e10f08e","source_text":"L^0(\\Bbb C)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:933","target_normalized_sha256":"fd1f4c15332cff00addab7bf4a662a0da663cb3de4849c8eee0ca997980e6fd9","target_text":"L^0_{\\Bbb C}","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"source-duplicate-word","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0224","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The active authority prose repeats 'then' consecutively; the derivative removes the duplicate while translating the sentence.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:937","source_text":"defined, then then u*(v*w)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:937","target_text":"terdefinisi, maka u*(v*w)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-monotonicity-direction","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0225","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"A nonnegative integrable approximate-identity kernel that rises toward zero on the negative half-line must fall away from zero on the positive half-line; the repeated non-decreasing condition is inconsistent with the intended unimodal hypothesis.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:987-988","source_text":"non-decreasing on \\coint{0,\\infty}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:987-988","target_text":"tak menaik pada \\coint{0,\\infty}","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-monotonicity-direction","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0226","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"This is the second occurrence of the same approximate-identity hypothesis in part (ii); it requires the same decreasing right-hand tail.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:992-993","source_text":"non-decreasing on \\coint{0,\\infty}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:992-993","target_text":"tak menaik pada \\coint{0,\\infty}","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-normalization","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0227","math_ordinal":721,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The kernel a exp(-a t) on t>=0 has unit mass; the printed factor 1/a gives mass 1/a^2 and cannot converge to f(x).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:1003","source_normalized_sha256":"4db640571a75b574cfde745ff3fcf0f05772df1f992baaeede65b3a6b1eef613","source_text":"\\Bover1a\\int_x^{\\infty}f(y)e^{-a(y-x)}dy","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:1003","target_normalized_sha256":"b7fe487673298b26c0f7fd6a4b5e105e7df7bfb6dd3afcabe74c7c17df11c25f","target_text":"a\\int_x^{\\infty}f(y)e^{-a(y-x)}dy","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
{"classification":"source-wrong-cross-reference-range","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0228","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Parts 255A(a)-(c) are one-dimensional, while the two-dimensional assertions are exactly 255A(d)-(e). Protected-reference ordinals 146-147 are ledgered by the unit validator.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt255.tex:1170","source_text":"255Ac-255Ad","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt255.tex:1170","target_text":"255Ad-255Ae","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S255"}
